# Suites and trials that the STM32-L476RG_raw trial target does not run, each with its reason.
# A skipped suite or trial is reported as skipped, never as passed. Keep the reasons honest:
#   target: -- the board target cannot run it (a missing runtime, no OS, a hardware limit)
#   driver: -- the board trial driver does not handle this suite's layout yet
#
#   <suite>                 <reason>     the whole suite
#   <suite>/<trial-stem>    <reason>     one trial
#
# Stage 1 (2026-11-07): `base`, then (same day, all green on the board: 4,064 trials) the int8..int64 and uint8..uint64 suites run. The runtime still lacks the message copier (ev_frame, described
# states, message_buffer/forward, reply_place), call/call_registered, actor failure handling and reports
# (a fault is process-fatal), supervisor restarts and the call_supervisor operations, recv, kill/fail,
# timers, priorities, policies, print_f64/f32/f16, the ordering identities and FFI (FFI landed 2026-11-10; see
# compiler/src/emitter/STM32-L476RG_raw/board/README.md, "Runtime: what is here"). Widen suite by suite:
# delete a suite's line here once the pieces it needs have landed and its trials pass.
#
# Sub-suites (subdirectories with their own Makefile) are skipped by the driver automatically.

bees_gaps_open_addition/monitor_down_delivered	target: the open defect this suite stages (README.md: a monitor never receives :down when the peer dies) fails here exactly as on the hosts ('no down message', status 1; checked 2026-11-10); the FFI trial of the suite passes (the board driver now stages the ffi_addition fixtures for a program suite's wrapper_meta, which was the E4030)
compile_defects_case_512_arms_addition        driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_ffi_same_unit_adapter_addition target: the staged front-end defect of this suite (README.md: E3010 'unused effect declaration: external_danger' on a call to a same-unit dangerous adapter) rejects the program here as on the hosts (checked 2026-11-10); the board's FFI runtime is not involved
compile_defects_float_literal_pattern_addition driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_float_record_field_binding_addition driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_float64_actor_message_addition driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_large_list_literal_frame_addition driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_migrate_actor_uint64_core_addition driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_nested_print_in_call_arg_addition driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_priority_queue_supervisor_addition driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_sum_binding_type_addition     driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_tagged_tuple_first_addition   driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_uint32_nested_literal_addition target: the staged front-end defect of this suite (README.md: E2003 on an integer literal nested in an expression on uint32 operands) rejects the program on this target's compiler as on the Mac (reported by the board finder, 2026-11-10); INTEGRATE_PENDING keeps the directory out of tree runs
compile_defects_trait_typed_record_call_x8_addition driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
compile_defects_tuple_rec_element_addition    driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
device_actor_addition                         target: the ESP32-S3 device-actor trials map ESP32-S3 windows and carry ESP32-S3_raw goldens only; this board runs its own twins, device_actor_stm32_addition (2026-11-10)
error_enforcement_addition                    driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
failure_reason_line_addition                  driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base until the STM32 runtime gains the message copier, call, failure reports and the print/ordering helpers they use
lexer_e0007_three_byte_file_addition          driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
ordered_data_structures                       driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base until the STM32 runtime gains the message copier, call, failure reports and the print/ordering helpers they use
region_hazards_open_addition                  driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base until the STM32 runtime gains the message copier, call, failure reports and the print/ordering helpers they use
region_hazards_open_errors_addition           driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
warning_enforcement_addition                  driver: not widened yet; stage 1 runs only base (compile-failure and diagnostics suites are widened after base passes)
transport_addition                            target: not run on this target by decision (the emitter now provides the transport builtins and wire formats)
ffi_addition/app_transport_tcp_loopback	target: boards run one app at a time; the loopback app is host-only
# ffi_addition (2026-11-10, group 7: rt_ffi.S) runs in app-directory mode with the board C fixtures of
# ffi_addition/fixtures_board_STM32-L476RG_raw.mk; only these programs are left out:
ffi_addition/dangerous_foreign_call_from_deep_stack	target: 100,000 Silica frames plus 150,000 C frames deep: megabytes of stack on a ~90 KB heap
ffi_addition/dangerous_spawn_thread_limit	target: spawns one OS thread per dangerous actor to hit the host's task limit; the board has no OS threads
ffi_addition/fault_before_main	target: hosted process-fatal path (ELF constructor probe, hosted silica_rt_ffi_guarded_* entries, C main)
ffi_addition/fault_inside_handler	target: hosted process-fatal path (C probe main, hosted fault-handler entries)
ffi_addition/foreign_fault_without_actor	target: hosted process-fatal path (C probe main, dladdr, hosted guarded entries)
ffi_addition/dangerous_unguarded_null_deref_abort	target: its probe is a C main() that faults outside any actor (host executable); the board has no such process
memory_region_addition/region_chain_free_walked	target: three 1.6 MB buffers (200000 int64) per region on a ~64 KB heap (untouched pages cost nothing on the host)
memory_region_addition/region_move_conditional	target: a 200000-int64 (1.6 MB) buffer on a ~64 KB heap (untouched pages cost nothing on the host)
memory_region_addition/region_move_pass_and_return	target: a 200000-int64 (1.6 MB) buffer on a ~64 KB heap (untouched pages cost nothing on the host)
memory_region_addition/region_move_pass_no_return	target: a 200000-int64 (1.6 MB) buffer on a ~64 KB heap (untouched pages cost nothing on the host)
memory_region_addition/region_scope_loop_release	target: a 200000-int64 (1.6 MB) buffer on a ~64 KB heap (untouched pages cost nothing on the host)
compiler_addition/substring_utf8_cursor	target: ~940 KB of never-freed intermediate strings on a ~64 KB heap (the host frees no strings either)
compiler_addition/string_literal_density	target: the image is 90 KiB of code and rodata for ~300 string cases; programs run from the 96 KiB SRAM1 and the link needs 16 KiB of heap
compiler_addition/region_grow	target: the 1000-deep recursion runs on the actor's chunked stack (~50 KB) beside the growing region, on a ~64 KB heap (heap: in use 60608 free 4480 at the abort)

# Actors stage, group 2 (failure handling and reports, rt_failure.S, 2026-11-09): kill / remove / stop_self /
# fail_self, traps (:language_error, actor_not_found ending the caller), death results, the failure report and
# its FailureReporter delivery, CPU faults in an actor (end that actor) and the main/actor split of every
# failure site. Lines left below name the group they still wait for.
# Actors stage, group 1 (messaging: call / call_registered / recv / the copier chain mode / back-pressure, 2026-11-09):
# actors_addition 370 of 388 pass on the board; the rest need later groups.
actor_registration_addition/registry_many_names	target: designed to be too big for this platform (the image does not fit the 96 KiB SRAM1: the link fails)
stack_budget_board_addition/actor_aux_overflow_ends_actor	target: needs the lowered stack reservation of stack_policy(n, ...) enforced (group 6; chunk growth stops only at heap exhaustion: :out_of_memory); the golden also spells (:explicit, :stack_exhausted), the pre-chunk-15 atom, where both board runtimes now report :reservation_exceeded
stack_budget_board_addition/actor_heap_exhausted_on_core1_aborts	target: needs a second core: the worker must run while main never yields (blank_lines(100000)); on one core it never runs and main exits 0
stack_budget_board_addition/actor_machine_overflow_ends_actor	target: needs the lowered stack reservation of stack_policy(n, ...) enforced (group 6; chunk growth stops only at heap exhaustion: :out_of_memory); the golden also spells (:explicit, :stack_exhausted), the pre-chunk-15 atom, where both board runtimes now report :reservation_exceeded
stack_budget_board_addition/thousand_actors_at_rest	target: 1,000 live actors need 224 KB of ACBs alone (208-byte ACB + block header each) on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap (heap exhausted); get_actor_memory_usage and the stack release policies are ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
stack_budget_board_addition/main_recursion_keeps_default	target: 1,500 nested frames in main need more than main's fixed 6 KiB machine stack (fault 70, cause 1006); main's stack is never enlarged on this board (Lee's ruling), so this trial cannot pass here; a per-image bound (main_stack_bound.py) would only report the overflow at build time
stack_budget_board_addition/actor_deep_recursion_grows	target: 2000 frames deep need more actor stack than both heap arenas hold (out of memory with SRAM1 heap 16 B and SRAM2 1,360 B free)
actor_stacks_addition/stack_deep_recursion_in_actor	target: these trials recurse far deeper than the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB SRAM2 chunk arena hold (out of memory); the ESP32-S3 skips the suite for the same reason
actor_stacks_addition/stack_keep_high_water_holds	target: these trials recurse far deeper than the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB SRAM2 chunk arena hold (out of memory); the ESP32-S3 skips the suite for the same reason
actor_stacks_addition/stack_keep_last_message_tracks_depth	target: these trials recurse far deeper than the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB SRAM2 chunk arena hold (out of memory); the ESP32-S3 skips the suite for the same reason
actor_stacks_addition/stack_release_when_idle_after_second	target: these trials recurse far deeper than the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB SRAM2 chunk arena hold (out of memory); the ESP32-S3 skips the suite for the same reason
actor_stacks_addition/stack_track_recent_peak_decays	target: these trials recurse far deeper than the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB SRAM2 chunk arena hold (out of memory); the ESP32-S3 skips the suite for the same reason
actor_stacks_addition/stack_lowered_reservation_exhausted	target: needs the lowered stack reservation of stack_policy(n, ...) enforced (decision pending with Lee; get_actor_memory_usage is ported, group 6, 2026-11-10); the failure path it ends in is in (group 2)
actor_stacks_addition/stack_reason_atoms_spelled_by_program	target: needs the lowered stack reservation of stack_policy(n, ...) enforced (decision pending with Lee; get_actor_memory_usage is ported, group 6, 2026-11-10); the failure path it ends in is in (group 2)
actor_stacks_addition/stack_reserve_failed_in_actor	target: needs a reservation check at spawn (stack_policy(2^62, ...) -> (:explicit, :stack_reserve_failed)); the board has no reservation step (chunks are taken lazily) and what 'reservation failed' means here is undecided (group 6)
actor_stacks_addition/stack_reserve_failed_in_main	target: needs a reservation check at spawn (in main the abort 'stack reservation failed', 71); the board has no reservation step (chunks are taken lazily) and what 'reservation failed' means here is undecided (group 6)
actor_stacks_addition/stack_many_idle_actors_hold_nothing	target: 1,000 live actors need 224 KB of ACBs alone (208-byte ACB + block header each) on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap (heap exhausted); get_actor_memory_usage and the stack release policies are ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
actor_stacks_addition/stack_release_on_return_shrinks	target: a 500,000-deep recursion (the golden's high water is over 4 MB) on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB chunk arena ((:explicit, :out_of_memory)); the ESP32-S3 skips the suite for the same reason; release policies are ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)


# Actors stage, group 3 (supervisors, rt_supervisors.S, 2026-11-09): restarts, intensity and breach, strategies, the
# deepest-first shutdown, start_child and every call_supervisor operation, exit reports, the trial hooks; registries
# sized per image (silica_registry_slots). supervisors_addition 135 of 143, supervisor_exit_reports_addition 6 of 13.
supervisors_addition/child_shut_down_with_supervisor	target: the board never preempts, so the busy slow child holds the one core until it ends and the supervisor cannot end while it runs (as on the ESP32-S3); supervisors_board_defects_addition/child_shut_down_with_supervisor_board is the board variant (passes)
supervisors_addition/phase_d_protocol_lifecycle_queries	target: main's frame is 6,704 bytes (the inline call_supervisor reply records) and main's fixed 6 KiB machine stack overflows at its prologue (fault 70, cause 1006); needs the per-image main stack bound (group 6) or a smaller frame
supervisors_addition/phase_d_protocol_lifecycle_queries_long_lived_binding	target: main's frame overflows main's fixed 6 KiB machine stack at its prologue (fault 70, cause 1006), as phase_d_protocol_lifecycle_queries; needs the per-image main stack bound (group 6)
supervisors_addition/supervisor_init_stack_exhausted_spawn_returns	target: needs the lowered stack reservation of stack_policy(n, ...) enforced (group 6): the init's recursion exhausts the heap instead ((:explicit, :out_of_memory)), so the report cannot be copied for the FailureReporter and is written on the console
stack_budget_board_addition/supervisor_end_frees_child_table	target: main's fixed 6 KiB machine stack overflows in a callee's prologue (fault 70, cause 1006; main's frame 3,296 bytes plus the helpers it calls); needs the per-image main stack bound (group 6). The supervisor part (rows freed, terminate/restart_child) is in
# carriers_addition (unskipped as a suite 2026-11-09, group 3): 24 of 62 pass; the rest, by reason:
carriers_addition/many_actors_one_carrier	target: 1,000 actors (224 KB of ACBs) on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap (heap exhausted); get_actor_memory_usage is ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
carriers_addition/workers_exhaustion_on_one_carrier_keeps_siblings	target: needs the lowered stack reservation of stack_policy(n, ...) enforced (256 KB reservation exhausted -> :reservation_exceeded; decision pending with Lee): without it the deep recursion exhausts the heap; get_actor_memory_usage is ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
carriers_addition/workers_zzzzz_idle_release_budget_bounds_burst	target: 4,000 actors with 64 KB reservations and the per-carrier idle-stack budget (SILICA_IDLE_STACK_BUDGET, a hosted feature) on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap (heap exhausted); :release_when_idle itself is ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
carriers_addition/workers_zzzzz_idle_release_exit_with_reporter	target: 20,000 idle actors on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap (heap exhausted); :release_when_idle itself is ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
carriers_addition/workers_zzzzz_idle_release_keeps_recently_mailed	target: a deep message holding over 1 MB of stack on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB chunk arena ((:explicit, :out_of_memory)); :release_when_idle itself is ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
carriers_addition/workers_zzzzz_idle_release_oldest_first	target: 401 actors and the per-carrier idle-stack budget (SILICA_IDLE_STACK_BUDGET, a hosted feature) on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap (heap exhausted); :release_when_idle itself is ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
carriers_addition/workers_zzzzz_idle_release_period_env	target: an actor holding over 1 MB of stack on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB chunk arena ((:explicit, :out_of_memory)), and the SILICA_IDLE_RELEASE_MS environment variable (a hosted feature); :release_when_idle itself is ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
carriers_addition/workers_two_carriers_interleaved_growth	target: two 500,000-deep recursions on the ~59 KB SRAM1 heap plus the 29 KB chunk arena ((:explicit, :out_of_memory)); the release policies are ported (group 6, 2026-11-10)
carriers_addition/workers_zpin_cast_stress_while_migrating	target: the emitter does not lower the actor_carrier_index prim for this target (the image does not assemble: 'unsupported int64 prim: actor_carrier_index')
